  "title": "Charles D Possible NDE",
  "date": "2025-03-05T20:32:56.000Z",
  "content": "I was 14 years old, and was down with a bad flu. As I lay on my bed, I started feeling tiny. I felt like my bedroom was the size of a large warehouse, compared to me. Then I was floating above my body, looking down at it curled on the bed. I started floating upward, and I could see the ceiling lamp from the side; like my eyes were exactly at the level of the ceiling. I could see the light bulb perfectly above the shade, and the graininess of the ceiling. This view was at an angle that I couldn't do physically because my head would have bump into the ceiling. My pupils were exactly on the ceiling surface. Then I was suddenly in my body again and no longer feeling tiny. I remember this event very clearly. <br><br> Since I was 17, I was diagnosed with a benign heart arrhythmia. Others in the family have it. However, whenever I get a flu, my heart beat goes way down sometimes very severely, like 30 bpm. This bradycardia also causes a severe sleep apnea causing me to stop breathing as soon as I fall asleep. This means a I have a night or two of insomnia. I believe my heart might have stopped for a while or gone into fibrillation when that OBE incident happened. <br><br><span class=\"m108",
